     only the gateway of its own assigned VLAN.  The two empty cells are the controls.
     They were measured in the same configuration, with the same instrument, within
     ninety seconds of the two full cells.  The untagged part of the case title is
     proved by `show vlan brief`: the same physical port is an untagged `(u)` member of
     both 362 and 363 at the same time, and `taggedVlansupplicantNum` is 0.
     The third column is an extra control that the design did not plan.  Client
     020d.b900.3362 could reach 10.38.22.66 in vlan 48 three times out of three in
     STEP 0, and zero times out of three here.  So the client did not only gain a VLAN.
     It also left the port's static access VLAN.  A test that only checked gateway
     reachability would not have shown that.

