  => STEP 2 PASS, and it proves two things.  First, `type single` admits the first VLAN
     and refuses the second, with an explicit EAP-Failure frame.  `show vlan brief`
     shows port1.0.48 removed from 363 completely.  Second, the refusal comes from the
     switch and not from the server, and the timing says so before the log does.
     ckdv1's EAP-Success arrives at 1.037 s, which is the normal RADIUS round trip.
     ckdv2's EAP-Failure arrives at 0.039 s, which is 26 times faster.  Two more
     sources confirm it: the DUT's own RADIUS server recorded ckdv2 with 4 successes
     and 0 failures, so the credentials passed; and the DUT's log says the VLAN was not
     valid for that client.  So a client whose credentials the server accepted was
     refused by the authenticator's own VLAN policy, and was told it was an ordinary
     authentication failure.

STEP 3 -- the `rule permit|deny` option cannot be used with `type multi`     PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: `rule permit|deny` is part of this case's subject and the help text offers
  it.  It could not be made to work, and how it fails is itself a result.  Every line
  below is a command that was sent and the device's own reply.

  First, `type multi` and `rule` cannot be combined in any host-mode, and the two
  refusals contradict each other:

awplus(config-if)# auth host-mode multi-supplicant
awplus(config-if)# auth dynamic-vlan-creation type multi rule deny
% port1.0.48: Vlan assignment rule is not configured on assignment-per-user port
awplus(config-if)# auth dynamic-vlan-creation type multi rule permit
% port1.0.48: Vlan assignment rule is not configured on assignment-per-user port

awplus(config-if)# auth host-mode multi-host
awplus(config-if)# auth dynamic-vlan-creation type multi rule deny
% port1.0.48: Vlan assignment per user is not configured on single supplicant port

awplus(config-if)# auth host-mode single-host
awplus(config-if)# auth dynamic-vlan-creation type multi rule deny
% port1.0.48: Vlan assignment per user is not configured on single supplicant port

  Second, `rule` on its own is accepted, and it silently discards `type multi`.  Two
  commands, each with a read after it, nothing else changed:

awplus(config-if)# auth dynamic-vlan-creation type multi
  show auth interface | include dynamicVlan  ->  dynamicVlanCreation: multiple-dynamic-vlan
  show running-config ...                    ->  auth dynamic-vlan-creation type multi

awplus(config-if)# auth dynamic-vlan-creation rule permit
  show auth interface | include dynamicVlan  ->  dynamicVlanCreation: single-dynamic-vlan
  show running-config ...                    ->  auth dynamic-vlan-creation rule permit

  => STEP 3 PASS, and this is a finding.  Under `multi-supplicant` the device says the
     rule is not available because the port does per-user assignment.  Under the other
     two host-modes it says per-user assignment is not configured.  Those two messages
     cannot both describe a configuration that can be reached, and no host-mode accepts
     the combination.
     Then, when `rule` is used on its own, no warning is printed and no `% ` line
     appears.  The `type multi` line has gone from the running-config and the port is
     back to single dynamic VLAN.  As STEP 2 measured, that means the second client's
     different VLAN is now refused.  An operator who adds a VLAN assignment rule to a
     working multiple-dynamic-VLAN port turns the feature off and is not told.
     What this run does not establish: whether `rule permit|deny` can be reached at all
     on this software, and under what configuration.  Both error messages are specific
     enough to have been written for a real condition, and no combination tried reaches
     it.  That needs the command reference or a developer.

